Container တစ်လုံးချင်းစီမှာ

IP address ရှိတယ်

Network interface (eth0) ရှိတယ်



| Network Type        | Description           | Use case      |
| ------------------- | --------------------- | ------------- |
| bridge              | Default local network | Simple apps   |
| user-defined bridge | Custom bridge + DNS   | ⭐ Recommended |
| host                | Host network direct   | Performance   |
| overlay             | Multi-host            | Swarm / K8s   |
| macvlan             | Real LAN IP           | Network lab   |


Default bridge vs User-defined bridge
❌ Default bridge (Not recommended)
Problems:

No automatic DNS
IP change easily
Manual linking

✅ User-defined bridge (Best practice)
Advantages:

Container name = DNS
Isolation
Custom subnet / IP


------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Demo 1: Default bridge (Problem demo)
docker run -d --name c1 nginx
docker run -it --name c2 busybox sh


Inside c2:

ping c1


❌ Fail (no DNS)

🧠 Teaching point

Default bridge = weak networking


------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Demo 1 Default bridge (Problem demo)

docker run -d --name c1 nginx
docker run -it --name c2 busybox sh

ping c1


------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Demo 2: User-defined bridge (Correct way)

docker network create school_net

docker run -d \
  --name web \
  --network school_net \
  nginx

docker run -it \
  --name client \
  --network school_net \
  busybox sh

ping web


Container name = hostname
DNS auto provided by Docker

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Custom IP & Subnet (Advanced but Important)

docker network create \
  --driver bridge \
  --subnet 172.25.0.0/16 \
  --gateway 172.25.0.1 \
  lab_net


docker run -d \
  --name app \
  --network lab_net \
  --ip 172.25.0.10 \
  nginx


------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Port Mapping vs Docker Network (Important Concept)


docker run -d \
  --name web \
  --network school_net \
  -p 8080:80 \
  nginx

Browser → Host:8080 → Container:80

docker inspect web | grep IPAddress

docker exec -it web ip addr

